  "notes": "Boot a FunHouse ROM from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released), the always-closed test-position switch 24 held closed and PinMAME's built-in mechanisms disabled; the scenario names no game. Leave the fresh-NVRAM loop with Escape (5), step past the game identification with Enter (8) to the main menu, go Up (7) to T. TESTS and Enter the test menu, go Up to T.6 GEN'L. ILLUM. and start it at ALL ILLUMINATION. In stop mode every Up press steps the selected circuit through eight brightness levels before moving on, so eight presses select each circuit in turn. On each circuit press Start (13): the ROM shows the circuit's wire colours, and each further Up shows its playfield and backbox connector pins, its fuse and its driver transistor. Escape returns to the circuit's brightness view, and the next eight Up presses select the next circuit; after the last circuit they step its brightness and return to ALL ILLUMINATION.",
  "version": 1
}
